## Interface: 120100
## Title: CoyFlightline Continued
## Notes: Adds a direction line to your minimap, zone map, and world map while flying
## Author: Coywolf (original), Tharavol (12.x update), Claude (Anthropic)
## Version: @project-version@
## SavedVariables: CoyFlightline_GlobalData
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\ability_mount_flyingcarpet
## Category-enUS: Map
## X-License: MIT

## X-ReleaseNotes: Draws a line from your character in the direction you are facing so you can see where a flight will actually take you, on three surfaces: the minimap, the zone map (Shift+M), and the world map (M). Each surface has its own toggle. By default the line is drawn while flying, while skyriding, and while travelling on a flight path, and each of those three triggers can be turned off independently; it is never drawn inside instances, because the game does not report your facing there. Line colour (white, yellow, cyan, magenta, green, or a custom RGB triple), thickness (1-6 px) and opacity (10-100%) are all configurable. Configure under Options > AddOns > CoyFlightline or with /cfl on its own; /cfl status prints current settings, /cfl help lists every command, and /cfl reset restores defaults. Source, issues and release notes: https://github.com/Tharavol/CoyFlightlineContinued

